      "title": "Cencora (COR) Up 3.8% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Continue?",
      "summary": "Cencora reported Q3 fiscal 2026 adjusted EPS of $4.48, beating consensus estimates by 2.5%, with 12% year-over-year earnings growth. Revenue rose 5.1% to $84.76 billion but slightly missed expectations. The company raised its fiscal 2026 adjusted EPS guidance to $17.75-$17.95 and increased operating income growth outlook to 13-14%. However, post-earnings estimates have trended downward, and the stock received a Zacks Rank #3 (Hold) rating.",
